{title: I Stand Amazed in the Presence}
{artist: Charles Gabriel}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
I [G]stand amazed in the [C]presence of [G]Jesus the Naza[D]rene,
and [G]wonder how he could [C]love me, a [G]sinner, con[D]demned, un[G]clean.

Chorus
[G]How marvelous! How [D]wonderful! And [G]my song shall ever [D]be:
[G]how marvelous! How [C]wonderful is my [G]Savior's [D]love for [G]me!

Verse 2
For [G]me it was in the [C]garden He pray'd "[G]Not my will, but [D]Thine;"
He [G]had no tears for His [C]own griefs, But [G]sweat drops of [D]blood for [G]mine.

Verse 3
In [G]pity angels beheld Him, [C]And came from [G]the world of [D]light
To [G]comfort Him in the [C]sorrows, He bore [G]for my [D]soul that [G]night.

Verse 4
When [G]with the ransomed in glory [C]His face [G]I at last shall [D]see,
'Twill [G]be my joy thro' [C]the ages, To sing [G]of His [D]love for [G]me.
